sensors.ID [SimTalk] - Tank
Returns the specified sensor of the Tank designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.sensors.ID(<Number>) → any
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
The number after the ID designates the unique identifier which Plant Simulation assigns when you create
the sensor.
Examples
MyTank.sensors.ID3.Front := true
var sensor := MyTank.sensors.ID2
sensor.Front := true
SimTalk
sensorID [SimTalk] - Tank
existsSensorID [SimTalk] - Tank
See also
Sensors [Tank]
